{
  "requirement": "Ordinary evidence validation, status inspection, and book rendering MUST continue\nto check evidence using the existing rules without invoking models, contacting\nproviders, or requiring authoring configuration or credentials. Missing or stale\nevidence MUST remain a validation failure rather than trigger authoring.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.authoring.deterministic_validation`.\n\n**Missing or stale evidence stays a validation failure and does not trigger authoring.**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[missing_or_stale_evidence_fails_validation_without_contacting_the_provider]` runs a missing case and a stale case.\n- Each case calls `validate_repository` and asserts an error naming the subject with \"missing for requirement\" or \"changed\".\n- Each case runs with a fully configured authoring file and with a bare `version = 1` file.\n- At the end it asserts that the evidence file is byte-identical to the original and that no usage state was recorded.\n\n**No models or providers are invoked.**\n- The same test binds a local listener as the provider endpoint.\n- It asserts at the end that `accept` returns `WouldBlock`, so validation, `status` and rendering never contacted it.\n- Together with the unchanged evidence and absent state file, this shows no authoring ran.\n\n**No authoring configuration or credentials are required.**\n- The `version = 1` config variant has no authoring settings.\n- The `status` and `mdbook` invocations run with `HABEAS_TEST_MODEL_KEY` removed and must succeed.\n- `ordinary_status_ignores_invalid_user_authoring_configuration` writes a malformed user config, and `status` still succeeds without creating state or changing evidence.\n- `status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_without_validating_authoring` and `validation_checks_workspace_common_config_without_loading_unused_authoring_settings` use an invalid but unused `[authoring]` section. They show that `status` and validation ignore it.\n\n**The existing rules still apply.**\n- `status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_without_validating_authoring` asserts that an invalid `habeas.toml` is reported as a finding. It also asserts that malformed evidence JSON is reported.\n- `status_applies_workspace_disallow_to_existing_evidence` asserts that a disallowed evidence path is reported as Invalid.\n- `validation_checks_workspace_common_config_without_loading_unused_authoring_settings` asserts the common-config errors.\n\n**Book rendering.** The missing/stale test runs the `habeas mdbook` preprocessor for both cases. It asserts success and that the output contains the subject. It does not assert any evidence finding in the rendered output. I treat that as acceptable because the requirement only says rendering must continue under the existing rules, without authoring.\n\nThe `{test}` markers are present on the relevant tests and on the `Fixture::run` helper.",
